# Sznyt Design — Claude Instructions

## About the project

Premium e-commerce shop for designer wooden picture frames. Real production business replacing sznytdesign.pl (WooCommerce). Adrian is the business owner and creative director — Claude Code acts as the developer, building what Adrian directs.

## Stack

- **Frontend**: React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 (Vite), port 5173
- **Backend**: Express + Prisma + PostgreSQL, port 3000
- **Run backend**: `npx tsx index.js` from `backend/` — NOT plain `node`
- **Seed database**: `npx tsx seed.js` from `backend/`

## Pages and routes

- `/` — Home (Hero with scroll indicator, ProductSection fetches from backend, BrandStatement, "why us" 3-column strip, Footer)
- `/sklep` — Shop listing (fetches all products, grid with hover image swap, philosophy strip, materials strip)
- `/sklep/:id` — ProductDetail (fetches single product, breadcrumb, image swap, stock, addItem, "← Odkryj całą kolekcję" link)
- `/o-nas` — About (hero, story split, process steps 01/02/03, two-button CTA)
- `/kontakt` — Contact (hero, two-column: form + contact info with links to FAQ/Zwroty)
- `/koszyk` — Cart (CartContext, quantity controls, shipping selector, address form with email field, regulamin checkbox, Stripe checkout)
- `/sukces` — OrderSuccess (card with order details + item breakdown, "Moje zamówienia" for signed-in users)
- `/admin` — AdminProducts (product table, Edytuj/Usuń, delete modal, ▲▼ sort order)
- `/admin/produkty/nowy` — AdminAddProduct (form, POST, navigate to /admin on success)
- `/admin/produkty/:id` — AdminEditProduct (pre-filled form, PUT, Anuluj/Potwierdź buttons)
- `/admin/zamowienia` — AdminOrders (order table with inline fulfillment status dropdown + tracking number input)
- `/moje-zamowienia` — MyOrders (protected, card list, product thumbnails, payment + fulfillment status dots, clickable rows)
- `/moje-zamowienia/:id` — OrderDetail (full order: products, payment method, shipping, fulfillment status + tracking number)
- `/regulamin` — Regulamin sklepu
- `/polityka-prywatnosci` — Polityka prywatności
- `/zwroty` — Zwroty i reklamacje (tabbed: Zwrot form + Reklamacja form)
- `/faq` — FAQ (accordion by category, links to /kontakt and /zwroty)
- Navbar + Footer render via `ShopLayout` layout route — admin routes sit outside it
- ScrollOnNav component in App.tsx scrolls to top on every route change
- ScrollToTop button: fixed bottom-right, appears after 300px scroll, brand-style (black border, inverts on hover)
- Active nav link highlighted in gold via `NavLink` from react-router-dom
- Navbar is sticky (`sticky top-0 z-40`), gains subtle shadow on scroll
- Hamburger menu animates to X on open (top/bottom lines rotate 45°, middle fades out)
- `src/components/ShopLayout.tsx` — layout component with `<Outlet />`, wraps all shop routes

## Database

- Prisma schema: `backend/prisma/schema.prisma`
- Product fields: id, name, tagline, description, price, imageUrl, lifestyleImageUrl, stock, sortOrder, createdAt
- Order fields: id, stripeSessionId, status, total, createdAt, customerEmail, userId, shippingMethod, shippingAddress (JSON), paymentMethod, fulfillmentStatus (default: "received"), trackingNumber
- OrderItem fields: id, quantity, price (snapshot), orderId, productId
- 2 products seeded: Ramka Szachownica (id:1), Ramka Corner Cut (id:2)
- Seed resets auto-increment sequence to 1 on each run

## Tailwind design tokens

- `bg-warm-white` — off-white background
- `text-near-black` / `bg-near-black` — dark sections and text
- `text-accent` / `bg-accent` — gold accent color
- `text-secondary-text` — muted grey text
- `border-borders` — subtle border color
- Dynamic values (e.g. background-image URLs) must use inline `style={}`, not Tailwind classes

## Typography patterns

- Headings: `font-cormorant font-light` (serif)
- Body/labels: `font-dm-sans` (sans-serif)
- Eyebrow labels: `font-dm-sans text-xs text-accent tracking-[0.3em] uppercase`

## Key code patterns

- Image hover swap: two `absolute inset-0` divs, opacity transition on `hovered` state
- Sub-components extracted when each instance needs its own state (e.g. ProductCard)
- Controlled forms: `value` + `onChange` per field, `e.preventDefault()` on submit
- Null guard: `if (!product) return <p>Ładowanie...</p>` before rendering fetched data
- `useParams()` always returns strings — use `Number(id)` when passing to API or state
- Modal pattern: `{isOpen && <><div overlay /><div modal /></>}` — siblings in fragment, overlay z-10, modal z-20
- Centering a fixed modal: `fixed top-1/2 left-1/2 -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2`
- After DELETE, filter deleted item from state: `setProducts(products!.filter((p) => p.id !== id))`
- `!` non-null assertion — TypeScript only, compiled away to JS, tells TS "trust me this isn't null"
- Active nav: `NavLink` with `className={({ isActive }) => isActive ? "text-accent" : "text-near-black hover:text-accent"}`
- Last page section should never be `bg-near-black` — same as footer, causes visual merge. Use `bg-warm-white border-t border-borders` instead.

## Hosting plan (decided)

- Frontend → Vercel
- Backend + PostgreSQL → Railway
- Domain registrar + email host → stays on cyberfolks.pl (kontakt@sznytdesign.pl)
- DNS records on cyberfolks will point to Vercel (frontend) and Railway (backend)
- Nodemailer SMTP credentials (cyberfolks) go in backend/.env — not yet added, needed for real email sending

## Cart / Context

- `src/context/CartContext.tsx` — CartProvider wraps App, exposes: items, addItem, removeItem, updateQuantity, totalItems
- Navbar shows cart icon with badge when totalItems > 0
- Cart state is in-memory only (resets on refresh)

## Auth (Clerk)

- Package: `@clerk/react` (NOT @clerk/clerk-react or @clerk/react-router)
- `ClerkProvider` wraps `<App />` in `main.tsx`, reads `VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` from root `.env`
- Clerk secret key in `backend/.env` as `CLERK_SECRET_KEY`
- Backend also needs `CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` (same value as frontend's `VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, without the `VITE_` prefix) — required by `@clerk/express`
- Polish localization: `@clerk/localizations` package, `plPL` passed as `localization` prop to ClerkProvider
- Navbar: `<Show when="signed-out">` → SignInButton (mode="modal"), `<Show when="signed-in">` → UserButton with custom menu item
- UserButton has custom "Moje zamówienia" link via `<UserButton.MenuItems><UserButton.Link>` pointing to `/moje-zamowienia`
- Guest checkout supported — userId is optional on Order model

## Shipping

- Shipping selector in Cart: InPost Paczkomat (20 PLN), InPost Kurier (25 PLN), DPD Kurier (25 PLN)
- Free shipping above 350 PLN subtotal
- Address form (all methods): firstName, lastName, email, street, postalCode, city, phone
- Paczkomat: additionally opens easyPack widget to select a parcel locker (code + city saved)
- `customer_email` passed to Stripe session from `shippingAddress.email`
- Furgonetka API for label generation — blocked until business registration (NIP required)

## Fulfillment status

- Stored on Order as `fulfillmentStatus` string, default: `"received"`
- Valid values: `received` → `processing` → `shipped` → `delivered`
- Admin updates via inline dropdown + tracking number input in AdminOrders (PATCH `/orders/:id/fulfillment`)
- When set to `shipped` with a tracking number: backend auto-sends shipping email to `customerEmail`
- Customer sees fulfillment status dot + label in MyOrders (card list) and OrderDetail
- Customer sees tracking number in OrderDetail when present

