8. **Deployment** — Vercel (frontend) + Railway (backend + DB) + cyberfolks DNS

## Architectural decisions (agreed)

- Stripe supports BLIK, Przelewy24, cards, bank transfers in Poland — enable in Stripe dashboard
- Stripe handles the payment page (hosted) — no custom payment UI needed
- Admin panel: build ourselves, not React Admin — familiar patterns, full control
- Auth: use Clerk — do NOT build custom auth for a real shop (security risk)
- SSR/Next.js: skip for now, revisit after launch if SEO becomes a problem. react-helmet-async covers basic needs.
- Shipping: Furgonetka.pl API (aggregates InPost, DPD, DHL etc. in one integration)
- Abandoned checkout recovery email: requires a job scheduler (node-cron / BullMQ / Inngest) — skip until post-launch
- This is a real production business (sznytdesign.pl), not just a portfolio piece — reliability and UX quality matter

## Git workflow

- Commit after every meaningful unit: one page, one component, one context, one bug fix
- Never one giant commit at the end of a session
- Never commit CLAUDE.md (it's in .gitignore)
- Commit messages start with a capital letter, e.g. "Fix bug", "Add feature", "Style component"

## How Adrian likes to work

- Claude Code is the developer. Adrian directs what to build, not how to build it.
- Briefly explain the plan (2-3 sentences) before building, then just do it
- After each task: one-line summary, how to test it, what's next
- Explain architecture and business trade-offs — skip syntax and code internals
- Always provide exact git commands to run — don't assume Adrian will do it unprompted
- This is a real production business — premium quality, no shortcuts

## Shared types

- `src/types.ts` — central types file
- All components import from here using `import type { X } from "../types"`
- `Product`: id, name, tagline, description, price, imageUrl, lifestyleImageUrl, stock
- `Order`: id, status, total, createdAt, shippingMethod, shippingAddress, paymentMethod, fulfillmentStatus, trackingNumber, items (OrderItem[])
- `AdminOrder`: id, stripeSessionId, status, total, createdAt, customerEmail, shippingMethod, shippingAddress, fulfillmentStatus, trackingNumber
- `OrderItem`: id, quantity, price, productId, product { name, imageUrl }
- `CartItem`: id, name, price, imageUrl, quantity, stock
- `CourierAddress`: firstName, lastName, email, street, postalCode, city, phone
- `PaczkomatPoint`: code, name, city?

## Current state

- All shop pages done and working end-to-end, fully responsive (mobile-first)
- Admin panel: list, add, edit, delete, orders with inline fulfillment/tracking, product sort order (▲▼)
- Stripe: checkout session with customer_email, webhook, Order saved to DB, confirmation email (SMTP not configured yet)
- Stripe webhook handles: `checkout.session.completed` → "paid", `checkout.session.expired` → "cancelled", `payment_intent.payment_failed` → "failed"
- Payment method (card/blik/p24) saved from PaymentIntent, shown in OrderDetail
- Fulfillment: 4-step flow (received/processing/shipped/delivered), tracking number, auto-email on shipped
- Clerk: sign in modal, Polish localization, UserButton with "Moje zamówienia" dropdown, userId wired to orders
- ScrollToTop button: fixed bottom-right, appears after 300px scroll
- Navbar sticky with scroll shadow; hamburger animates to X
- Active nav link highlighted via NavLink
- Honeypot spam protection on Contact, Zwrot, Reklamacja forms (`_hp` field)
- Legal pages: /regulamin, /polityka-prywatnosci, /zwroty (with forms), /faq (accordion)
- Zwroty/reklamacja forms: send emails via backend /zwrot and /reklamacja endpoints
- FAQ: /zwroty links are proper React Links (not plain text paths)
- Footer: dark bg, 3 link columns, real routes

