## Key reminders

- Backend must be run with `npx tsx index.js` — NOT plain `node`
- After Prisma schema changes: run both `npx prisma migrate dev` AND `npx prisma generate`
- Stripe CLI: run `stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/webhook` in separate terminal when testing payments
- Stripe success_url uses http://localhost in dev — Chrome may show SSL error; manually navigate to http://localhost:5173/sukces as workaround
- Clerk package is `@clerk/react` — NOT `@clerk/clerk-react` or `@clerk/react-router`
- Backend Clerk requires both `CLERK_SECRET_KEY` and `CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY` in `backend/.env`
- `ADMIN_USER_ID` must be set in both root `.env` (as `VITE_ADMIN_USER_ID`) and `backend/.env` (as `ADMIN_USER_ID`)
- Furgonetka requires NIP/business registration — skip until Adrian has that set up
- Guest checkout supported — userId is optional on Order model
- After creating production Stripe webhook, manually add events: `checkout.session.completed`, `checkout.session.expired`, `payment_intent.payment_failed`

